  "id": "vocal-communication",
  "term": "vocal communication",
  "definition": "Vocal communication is the use of sounds or calls to exchange information with others. In the source packet, it is described as serving functions such as avoiding conflict, supporting survival, mating, and parental care, and it can range from simple to complex repertoires with distinctive call patterns.",
